WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.590 --> 00:00:04.730
Here's a spoiler for you: Try as you might,
you can't please everyone.

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:08.630
It's something that Game of Thrones showrunners
David Benioff and D.B. Weiss have learned

00:00:08.630 --> 00:00:13.670
the hard way, as the final season of the pop
culture phenomenon has infuriated and disappointed

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:15.640
legions of fans and critics around the world.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:20.720
In fact, so many people were upset by the
final season that over a million viewers signed

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:26.230
an online petition calling for HBO to remake
all six episodes with different storylines

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:27.400
and a new team of writers.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.340
So what does the cast of Game of Thrones think
about all this?

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:35.320
Well, Isaac Hempstead Wright, who plays the
newest king of Westeros, Bran Stark, told

00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:38.510
The Hollywood Reporter that he for one thought
the petition was absurd.

00:00:38.510 --> 00:00:42.900
"I saw today there's a petition to redo the
ending […] It's just absurd.

00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:44.160
I can't even fathom it.

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:47.360
[...] It's ridiculous that people think they
can just demand a different ending because

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.520
they don't like it."

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.579
Hempstead Wright admitted that he took the
petition personally, in part because he just

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:55.260
doesn't agree with people who think the final
season was bad.

00:00:55.600 --> 00:01:00.820
"What people were hoping for is an Avengers-esque
thing where all the superpowers are explained

00:01:00.820 --> 00:01:03.560
and everybody comes together and there's a
big team effort.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:05.220
Game of Thrones isn't like that.

00:01:05.220 --> 00:01:06.939
It's unpredictable by nature.

00:01:06.939 --> 00:01:10.950
[...] In my opinion, it's a great ending […] I
don't think it's some plot twist to be shocking

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:11.940
for the sake of shocking.

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.300
I think it's a genuine character development."

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:18.299
In fact, he thinks people getting angry at
the ending is just further proof of how good

00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:19.299
the show was.

00:01:19.299 --> 00:01:22.650
"The fact that characters are not doing what
people want them to do?

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:23.650
It's a good thing.

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:27.259
The fact that people are getting pissed off
and having a big emotional response?

00:01:27.259 --> 00:01:29.840
That's the reason why Game of Thrones is successful.

00:01:29.840 --> 00:01:31.950
It doesn't do what everyone wants them to
do."

00:01:31.950 --> 00:01:36.289
Of course, the interview with Hempstead Wright
was published before the season finale aired

00:01:36.289 --> 00:01:37.640
on Sunday, May 19.

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:41.719
At the time the petition was created, fans
were still infuriated over the events of the

00:01:41.719 --> 00:01:46.979
show's penultimate episode, "The Bells," which
saw fan favorite Daenerys Targaryen go completely

00:01:46.979 --> 00:01:50.990
mental and mass-murder tens if not hundreds
of thousands of people for what seemed like

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:51.940
no good reason.

00:01:52.209 --> 00:01:56.799
The finale, though, has by and large received
kinder critical and fan reviews.

00:01:56.799 --> 00:02:01.329
Though it didn't fully satisfy everyone, the
death of Daenerys at Jon Snow's hand, and

00:02:01.329 --> 00:02:06.219
the subsequent crowning of Bran the Three-Eyed
Raven as king of the Six Kingdoms was met

00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:08.319
more with resigned shrugs than blinding rage.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:13.620
And at least Benioff and Weiss wrote and directed
the finale themselves, making sure that the

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:17.840
final responsibility for bringing the series
home rested on the right shoulders.

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:20.540
After all, as Ned taught Bran way back in
the series premiere,

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.340
"The man who passes the sentence should swing
the sword."

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:29.580
So while it's true that few fans got everything
they wanted out of the finale, the fact that

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:33.080
nobody's completely satisfied might actually
be a good thing.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:33.700
Just ask Tyrion:

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:38.900
"No one is very happy, which means it's a
good compromise I suppose."

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:44.660
Indeed, the last episode of Game of Thrones
took some interesting turns and placed power

00:02:44.660 --> 00:02:46.439
into the hands of a few unexpected people.

00:02:46.439 --> 00:02:51.099
It also gave the members of the Stark family
a relatively happy ending, something nobody

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.620
could have expected after all the losses they
suffered in previous seasons.

00:02:54.989 --> 00:02:59.599
And the divisive final season doesn't change
the fact that so many people genuinely love

00:02:59.599 --> 00:03:04.049
the show, or that Thrones will go down in
history as one of the most popular television

00:03:04.049 --> 00:03:05.380
series of this generation.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:07.850
As the new king of Westeros said,

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.560
"If people really, really hate this season?

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:11.340
Then so be it.

00:03:11.520 --> 00:03:15.989
But it's been seven or eight years of absolutely
brilliant television that captivated the world

00:03:15.989 --> 00:03:20.020
[...] I think people will remember it as a
fabulous journey to have been a part of, no

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:21.820
matter their opinion on the ending."

